## Mandatory engineering rules

- Existing customer records and files survive routine upgrades; no resets or destructive migrations without special authorization.
- Every company is explicitly identified, even in a dedicated single-company installation.
- Platform administrators/technicians/users have different grants from company administrators/personnel. Platform technicians support **only assigned companies** through audited, server-enforced permissions.
- UI/Admin UI do not access database directly when a trusted service/repository boundary exists. Domain/business operations own rules; Data owns schema/migrations.
- Preserve API/contracts and minimize affected deployment units where architecture permits.
- Every change has an accountable agent owner, tests, documentation and independent QA when risk warrants. Coordinator assigns anything unowned.

